<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Aramaeans</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Aramaeans were a Semitic-speaking people of ancient <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesopotamia">Mesopotamia</a> who formed numerous small states in the early first millennium BCE. Many settled in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylonia">Babylonia</a>, where they mixed with Chaldean and Babylonian populations. Their language, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aramaic">Aramaic</a>, spread widely and became a common language of the Neo-Babylonian or <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chaldean-empire">Chaldean Empire</a>.</p></div>
